    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d704">

                <pb facs="0525" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/505: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-31T18:00:00+08:00">October 31, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 31—10:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese military and naval authorities are proceeding in an apparently orderly
                    manner to occupy property for their use. Representatives from <hi
                        rendition="#italic">gendarmerie</hi> headquarters called yesterday and were
                    allowed to copy data from the map in possession of this office showing American
                    owned property insofar as it had been reported to this office. A memorandum was
                    handed to them at the same time stating that the map did not purport to show all
                    American owned or occupied property and making reservation of rights.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
